el through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Wh-Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use Wh-questions to get specific information. You can use Wh-question words in questions with modals like <span class=\"strong\">can</span>.<br>When you ask Wh-questions with verbs, you use <span class=\"strong\">do</span> (except for the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be</span>) or a modal like <span class=\"strong\">can</span>.<br> Words can be placed after the question word to make it more specific, like <span class=\"italic\">What kind of</span>  ... or <span class=\"italic\">What flavor of ...</span> <br><br>Verbs like <span class=\"italic\">want</span> and <span class=\"italic\">prefer</span> are followed by another verb in the infinitive form (to + verb)."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Wh-Question Word\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Specific Information\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" What\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a thing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a time or date\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Where \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a place\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Why\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a reason\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Who\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a person\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When can you come?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Where do you want to go?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What do you prefer to do?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What kinds of ice cream do you have?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Where are you going?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to share"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give part of what you have to another person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would prefer to share a dessert."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to order dessert."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "frozen yogurt"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a cold dessert,  similar to ice cream, that is made of yogurt and other dairy products"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What kind of frozen yogurt do you have?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "strawberry"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small sweet red fruit that grows in a bush and has small seeds"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We have orange or strawberry frozen yogurt."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "maple syrup"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a sweet liquid made from maple trees"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would like to try the maple syrup pudding!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rich"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes a food that is very heavy or sweet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The desserts here are so rich."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "piece"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a part of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Would you like a piece of cake?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn3le07ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose 5 desserts for the menu."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe each desserts in 2 - 3 sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Draw or find images on the internet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Role-play a situation in a restaurant. A partner asks questions and orders a dessert."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I prepare a menu."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about desserts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask questions about desserts and answers questions."}]}], "type": "sena"}